{
  "id": "tracing-tracing",
  "slug": "tracing",
  "title": "Tracing",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-distributed-tracing",
      "heading": "What is Distributed Tracing?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In a microservices architecture, a single user request can pass through multiple microservices. Tracing the path of a request becomes essential for:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Debugging issues",
            "Understanding application flow",
            "Identifying bottlenecks",
            "Monitoring service interactions"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 32,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "problem-tracking-requests-across-microservices",
      "heading": "Problem: Tracking Requests Across Microservices",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "example",
          "heading": "Example:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A request to view a customer's profile may touch the following microservices:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "infytel-customer",
                "infytel-friend-family",
                "infytel-plan"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "In larger systems, hundreds of services might be involved."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Solution: Use Spring Cloud Sleuth and Zipkin for end-to-end request tracing."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 35,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spring-cloud-sleuth",
      "heading": "Spring Cloud Sleuth",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "definition",
          "heading": "Definition:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Spring Cloud Sleuth is a Spring Cloud module for distributed tracing. It helps log and track requests across microservices using Trace IDs and Span IDs."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 25,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "core-concepts",
          "heading": "Core Concepts:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Concept",
                "Description"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "traceId",
                  "Unique ID assigned to a request. Same across all services it touches."
                ],
                [
                  "spanId",
                  "Unique ID for a specific segment (or hop) of the trace."
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 27,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "example",
          "heading": "Example:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "If a request touches 3 microservices:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "One traceId (e.g., abcd1234)",
                "Three spanIds (one for each microservice)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "[infytel-customer, abcd1234, 1a2b3c4d, false]\n[infytel-friend-family, abcd1234, 4d3c2b1a, false]\n[infytel-plan, abcd1234, 5e6f7g8h, false]",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "First: service name",
                "Second: trace ID",
                "Third: span ID",
                "Fourth: export status (to Zipkin)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 30,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "how-to-use-sleuth",
          "heading": "How to Use Sleuth",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": true,
              "items": [
                "Add Dependency to pom.xml in each microservice: <dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-sleuth</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
                "Log Format: Sleuth automatically appends trace info to log statements. Example Log: 2025-05-30 12:34:56.123  INFO [infytel-customer, abcd1234, 1a2b3c4d, false] ..."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 31,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zipkin-distributed-tracing-ui",
      "heading": "Zipkin: Distributed Tracing UI",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "definition",
          "heading": "Definition:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Zipkin is a distributed tracing system that collects and visualizes trace data from multiple microservices."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "It provides:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "A UI to trace requests",
                "Timeline views",
                "Latency and performance monitoring"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Microservices/Tracing/Tracing/0425dc1d-105b-4173-a854-6a0ffa9831ca.png",
              "alt": "image.png",
              "originalPath": "Tracing/0425dc1d-105b-4173-a854-6a0ffa9831ca.png"
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 28,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "how-zipkin-integrates-with-sleuth",
          "heading": "How Zipkin Integrates with Sleuth:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Sleuth generates tracing info.",
                "Zipkin collects and stores it for analysis.",
                "Sleuth sends trace data to the Zipkin server (configured by you)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 22,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "zipkin-features",
          "heading": "Zipkin Features",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Web UI available at: http://localhost:9411",
                "Query traces by: ",
                "Displays: "
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 9,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "setting-up-zipkin",
      "heading": "Setting Up Zipkin",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "1-create-a-new-spring-boot-project-infytel-zipkin",
          "heading": "1. Create a new Spring Boot project: infytel-zipkin",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2-add-dependencies",
          "heading": "2. Add Dependencies:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependency>\n    <groupId>io.zipkin.java</groupId>\n    <artifactId>zipkin-autoconfigure-ui</artifactId>\n    <scope>runtime</scope>\n</dependency>\n<dependency>\n    <groupId>io.zipkin.java</groupId>\n    <artifactId>zipkin-server</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "3-add-annotation-in-main-class",
          "heading": "3. Add Annotation in Main Class:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@SpringBootApplication\n@EnableZipkinServer\npublic class InfytelZipkinApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(InfytelZipkinApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "4-configure-application-port-in-applicationproperties",
          "heading": "4. Configure Application Port (in application.properties):",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "server.port=9411",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "connecting-microservices-to-zipkin",
      "heading": "Connecting Microservices to Zipkin",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "1-add-dependency-to-each-microservice",
          "heading": "1. Add Dependency to Each Microservice:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-zipkin</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2-configure-zipkin-server-url-in-each-microservice",
          "heading": "2. Configure Zipkin Server URL (in each microservice):",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "spring.zipkin.base-url=http://localhost:9411/",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "blockquote",
              "text": "✅ This can also be stored in a centralized cloud-config file for consistency."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 13,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
